The results show that increasing the Winkler stiffness parameter (
k w
) from 0 to 100 leads to a consistent rise in the dimensionless frequencies, with an increase of approximately 2.4% to 3.0%. This stiffening effect is slightly more noticeable for thinner plates. In addition, the dimensionless frequencies increase significantly with the thickness ratio (
h a
/
). Thicker plates exhibit higher dimensionless frequencies due to their greater bending stiffness. These observations demonstrate the combined influence of the foundation stiffness and the plate thickness on the dynamic behavior of the plate-foundation system.
